Set the version of a saved preset record

The preset save built the settings from the widgets and left the version
field of that record at whatever the stack held. The dialog keeps the
record in memory, and it tests the version to decide whether the window
manager settings load. That test therefore read an indeterminate value.

Set the version of the record to the version of this build. The written
file carries the same version, so a later read of the file gives the
value that the record holds.

The change sits on the branch work/presets of the local tree, as commit 3 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 6b746070..62144828 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -2595,6 +2595,21 @@ void QtCurveConfig::savePreset()
         KMessageBox::error(this, i18n("Sorry, failed to save preset"));
 }
 
+/**
+ * \brief Give the version of this build in packed form.
+ *
+ * \return The version of this build, packed as the settings reader packs the
+ *         version of a settings file. The value is 0 when the version string
+ *         does not hold three numbers.
+ */
+static int packedVersion()
+{
+    const QStringList ver(QString::fromLatin1(qtcVersion()).split('.'));
+
+    return (ver.count() >= 3 ?
+            qtcMakeVersion(ver[0].toInt(), ver[1].toInt(), ver[2].toInt()) : 0);
+}
+
 bool QtCurveConfig::savePreset(const QString &name)
 {
     if(!kwin->ok())
@@ -2607,6 +2622,7 @@ bool QtCurveConfig::savePreset(const QString &name)
     Options opts;
 
     setOptions(opts);
+    opts.version=packedVersion();
 
     if(IMG_FILE==opts.bgndImage.type)
         opts.bgndImage.pixmap.file=saveThemeFile(bgndImageDlg->fileName(), BGND_FILE IMAGE_FILE, fname);
